/*Q1. Emma is managing a library system where she needs to update the due dates of borrowed books. She requires an application that allows her
to update the due date of a specific book by its index. However, she wants the application to handle situations where users enter invalid
indices.
Write a Java program to assist Emma in updating the due dates of books in the library system.
Input Format:

• The first line contains a positive integer representing the number of books in the library.

• The second line contains space-separated strings representing the titles of the books.

• The third line contains space-separated strings representing the due dates of the books.

• The fourth line contains an integer representing the index of the book for which the due date needs to be updated.

• The fifth line contains a string representing the new due date for the book.

Output Format:

• If the provided index is valid, print the updated due dates of all books on a single line, separated by a space. The due date at the
specified index must be replaced with the new due date. Print a space after each due date, including the last one, followed by a
newline.

• If the provided index is invalid (negative or greater than or equal to the number of books), print the following error message on a
separate line:

Error: Index is out of bounds
Note: The book index is zero-based. Only the due date at the specified index should be updated; all other due dates must remain unchanged.
*/
import java.util.Scanner;
 
public class LibraryDueDates {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        int n = Integer.parseInt(sc.nextLine().trim());
        String[] titles = sc.nextLine().trim().split("\\s+");
        String[] dueDates = sc.nextLine().trim().split("\\s+");
        int index = Integer.parseInt(sc.nextLine().trim());
        String newDate = sc.nextLine().trim();
        try {
            if (index < 0 || index >= n) {
                throw new ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException("Index is out of bounds");
            }
            dueDates[index] = newDate;
            StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();
            for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
                sb.append(dueDates[i]).append(" ");   // space after every date
            }
            System.out.println(sb);
        } catch (ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException e) {
            System.out.println("Error: Index is out of bounds");
        }
        sc.close();
    }
}
